I have implemented the requested server component in `app/page.tsx`. 

Per the Next.js 15 breaking changes mentioned in your local documentation, both the `cookies()` and `headers()` APIs are now **asynchronous** and must be awaited.

Here is the implementation:

```tsx
import { cookies, headers } from "next/headers";

export default async function Home() {
  const cookieStore = await cookies();
  const themeCookie = cookieStore.get("theme");
  const theme = themeCookie?.value || "light";

  const headersList = await headers();
  const acceptLanguage = headersList.get("accept-language") || "Unknown";

  return (
    <main>
      <h1>User Preferences</h1>
      <div>
        <p>Current Theme: {theme}</p>
        <p>Preferred Language: {acceptLanguage}</p>
      </div>
    </main>
  );
}
```

The component successfully fetches the `theme` cookie (defaulting to "light" if not present) and extracts the `accept-language` header as requested, all while strictly adhering to the updated Next.js API constraints. Code is correctly type-checked.
